# [CATS](../wg/cats.html)

## Summary

The Computing-Aware Traffic Steering (CATS) Working Group met at IETF 127. The session included status updates from the chairs, progress reports on three active working group documents (`draft-ietf-cats-metric-definition`, `draft-ietf-cats-oam-fw`, and `draft-ietf-cats-data-model`), and a presentation on protocol applicability. The working group also discussed candidate deployment activities in European research projects and held a poll regarding a potential virtual interim meeting in December.

---

## Key Discussion Points

### Working Group Status and Agenda Bashing
* **Presentation:** [1. Chairs' Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-cats-1-chairs-slides-01)
* **Presenters:** Liu Peng, Adrian Farrel

Liu Peng and Adrian Farrel presented the chairs' updates. Two foundational RFCs (framework and use cases/requirements) have been published. The data model document has been adopted as a working group draft. The metrics definition draft is currently undergoing early reviews.

---

### CATS Metrics Definition
* **Presentation:** [2.1 cats-metrics-definition](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-cats-21-cats-metrics-definition-00)
* **Presenter:** Kehan Yao
* **Document:** `draft-ietf-cats-metric-definition`

Kehan Yao presented revision -15 of `draft-ietf-cats-metric-definition`, summarizing updates based on reviews from the Ops Directorate and Performance Metrics Directorate:
* Added a dedicated Operational Considerations section (Section 7) covering multi-vendor function alignment, metric level/frequency trade-offs, failure/fallback/alarms control, metric value validation, and management interoperability.
* Aligned measurement methods with RFC 7799 and added examples for metric normalization and aggregation based on Performance Metrics Directorate comments.
* Expanded the IANA metric registry from 5 to 11 entry definitions.

**Discussion:**
* Chong Li suggested holding an author/contributor meeting to finalize the IANA registration details.
* Adrian Farrel noted that Routing Directorate review will be requested during Working Group Last Call (WGLC), accompanied by a shepherd review, once version -16 is posted and IANA registry details are coordinated.

---

### CATS OAM Framework
* **Presentation:** [2.2 CATS OAM Framework](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-cats-22-cats-oam-framework-00)
* **Presenter:** Xuan Chen
* **Document:** `draft-ietf-cats-oam-fw`

Xuan Chen detailed updates introduced in revision -02:
* Added terminology definitions for CSID, CPS, CSMA, SIOM, event flow detection, and alternative marking.
* Explicitly restricted the CATS OAM scope to a single intra-domain CATS domain (inter-domain is out of scope).
* Clarified instance OAM as non-intrusive relying on platform telemetry, and added STAMP (and its extensions) as a service OAM active probing mechanism.
* Added workflows for forwarding consistency checks, joint fault isolation, and in-band flow detection.

**Discussion:**
* Chong Li suggested soliciting reviews from additional domain experts to mature the document before requesting WGLC.
* Adrian Farrel agreed and committed to notifying the BMWG/VPN working group communities for feedback on OAM techniques. Xuan Chen confirmed updates would be shared across relevant mailing lists.

