### CATS Protocols Applicability
* **Presentation:** [3. CATS Protocols Applicability](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-cats-3-cats-protocols-applicability-00)
* **Presenter:** Linda Dunbar

Linda Dunbar presented the updated protocol applicability draft, incorporating feedback from AD Jim Guichard:
* Reorganized the draft to state explicit CATS requirements across protocol areas (data plane, control plane, management plane) rather than just stating general protocol suitability.
* Included systemic overview diagrams for centralized vs. distributed metric distribution and path selection.
* Added requirement frameworks for BGP (candidate identity/semantics, metric lifecycle/scale, distribution/selection), PCE, BGP SR, BGP FlowSpec, service configuration/management, and OAM.

**Discussion:**
* Kehan Yao noted that standard ping/traceroute tools measure general network metrics but may be insufficient for CATS metrics, offering to contribute text based on performance directorate feedback.
* Adrian Farrel raised the topic of service/entity discovery parameters (e.g., contact instances, agent stability, scope), comparing discovery requirements to work in other groups (such as DAWN/DON). Linda Dunbar noted ongoing discussions with IDR chairs regarding metadata path attributes and wide community containers for advertising prefix capabilities.

